# Data tables — everything tabular/binary in data/ stays local.
# The schema/config JSONs (category_taxonomy, global_filters, master_metadata*)
# are the deliberate exception and stay tracked.
data/*.csv
data/*.tsv
data/*.xlsx
data/*.xls
# ...except the design workbook: category counts, the reviewed cat_4 folding
# behind category_taxonomy.json, per-category field coverage, and the pipeline
# spec extract_features.py was written from. Curated by hand, not generated.
!data/Item Features.xlsx
data/*.pkl
data/*.parquet
data/*.feather
# Shared, cross-model snapshot artifacts (item_asins.npy, node_of_item.npy,
# tower_pairs_*.parquet) plus the cross-model serving layer.
data/tower/

# Each model's own generated output (arrays, trained checkpoints,
# recommendations) now lives alongside that model's code, not under data/ --
# still entirely regenerable, still never committed, same convention as
# data/tower/ above, just one level up per model.
TTN/generated/
SigLIP2/generated/
SigLIP2/image_cache/
SigLIP2/_image_download_cache/
Popularity/generated/

# Trained model checkpoints, anywhere in the repo -- except a deliberately
# imported, promoted checkpoint this repo doesn't train itself (see
# SigLIP2/adapter_checkpoint/README.md for provenance).
*.pt
!SigLIP2/adapter_checkpoint/*.pt

data/*.npy
data/*.npz
data/*.h5
data/*.hdf5
data/*.db
data/*.sqlite
data/*.sqlite3
data/*.zip
data/*.gz
# Pickle backups (df_features.pkl.bak-YYYYMMDD)
data/*.pkl.bak*

# Raw source dataset (~16 GB) — the schema/config JSONs in data/ stay tracked
data/meta_Home_and_Kitchen.json

# Derived from df_features.pkl by data_creation/build_image_url_cache.py --
# regenerable, not config, unlike the other tracked data/*.json files.
data/asin_image_urls.json

# Generated tables anywhere in the repo, not just data/. The rules above are
# path-scoped, so a pickle or CSV written next to a notebook — e.g. a pair
# table saved into complementary_cats_pairs/ or ttn/ — would otherwise be
# committed. It is still a generated data table and still stays local.
*.pkl
*.csv
*.parquet

# Explicitly called out despite already matching *.parquet above: this one's
# 142 MB (over GitHub's 100MB push limit) and lives inside the imported
# checkpoint's own folder (SigLIP2/checkpoints/pilot_200k/), not the usual
# Model/generated/ location every other generated table uses -- worth a
# named reminder of why, not just silent coverage by the blanket rule.
SigLIP2/checkpoints/pilot_200k/recommendations/full_catalog_top40.parquet

# IDE
.idea/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Python
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
